# two coronal series (G80's rule; p41 section 0 anchor (ii)); the decoder's header scan and pixel read are memoised PER STUDY
# (thread-local, opened and closed by load()), so a frame both stacks pick is decoded once.  Outside load() the decoder's own
# functions run.  The returned arrays are never written in place (build_study and build_study_canon make new arrays).
import threading as _threading
